<title>NEW ZEALAND: POLL-NZ June qtr employment seen dipping further.</title>
<headline>POLL-NZ June qtr employment seen dipping further.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is the result of</p>
<p>a survey of 13 economists for the June quarter New Zealand</p>
<p>Household Labour Force Survey data due on Tuesday at 10.45 a.m.</p>
<p>NZT, 2245 GMT (figures are percentage changes).</p>
<p>					  AVG</p>
<p>INDICATOR		  PERIOD   F/CAST  PREV  MEDIAN   RANGE</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>HLFS</p>
<p>S/adj unemployment	  qtr   6.92    6.4    6.9     6.7-7.3</p>
<p>s/adj employment growth   qtr  -0.15   -0.1   -0.2    -0.4-0.4</p>
<p>s/adj employment growth   yr    0.05    1.1   +0.1    -0.2-0.6</p>
<p>Participation rate		 65.65   65.7   65.6    65.3-66.0</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>The following organisations participated in the poll: AMP Investments,  ANZ Bank, ASB, Bancorp, Bankers Trust NZ, BNZ, Deutsche Morgan Grenfell,  Doyle Paterson Brown, Garlick &amp; Co, Merrill Lynch, National Bank,  UBS Australia,  WestpacTrust.</p>
<p>-- Wellington newsroom 64 4 4734 746</p>
<p>e-mail wellington.newsroom@reuters.com</p>
